      "num": "01",
      "en": "China is widely known for its ancient civilisation which has continued all the way through into modern times, {despite} the many ups and downs in its history. There are many reasons why this has been possible, but one of the main factors has been the Chinese writing {system}. At the beginning, written Chinese was a picture-{based} language. It dates back several thousand years to the use of *longgu* — animal bones and shells on which symbols were carved by ancient Chinese people. Some of the ancient symbols can still be seen in today's *hanzi*. By the Shang {Dynasty} (around 1600–1046 BCE), these symbols had become a well-developed writing {system}. Over the years, the {system} developed into different forms, as it was a time when people were divided geographically, leading to many varieties of dialects and characters. This, however, changed under Emperor Qinshihuang of the Qin {Dynasty} (221–207 BCE). Emperor Qinshihuang united the seven {major} states into one unified country where the Chinese writing {system} began to develop in one direction. That writing {system} was of great importance in uniting the Chinese people and culture. Even today, no matter where Chinese people live or what {dialect} they speak, they can all still communicate in writing. Written Chinese has also become an important {means} by which China's present is connected with its past. People in modern times can read the {classic} works which were written by Chinese in ancient times. The high {regard} for the Chinese writing {system} can be seen in the development of Chinese characters as an art form, known as Chinese {calligraphy}, which has become an important part of Chinese culture. Today, the Chinese writing {system} is still an important part of Chinese culture. As China plays a greater role in {global} affairs, an increasing number of international students are beginning to {appreciate} China's culture and history through this amazing language.",
      "cn": "中国，因其一路绵延至今的古代文明而著称于世，尽管历史跌宕起伏（依然如此）。\"这种情况之所以可能出现\"的原因有很多，但主要因素之一就是汉语书写体系。 起初，书面汉字是一种基于图形的语言。它可以追溯至数千年前对\"龙骨\"（*longgu*）的使用——就是古代中国人刻下符号的动物骨头和甲壳。这些古代符号中的一部分在今天的汉字中依然可以看到。 到了商朝（大约公元前 1600—1046 年），这些符号已经演变为一套成熟完善的书写体系。经过了好些年，这套体系发展成了不同的形式，乃是由于当时人们在地理上是分隔开的，就导致方言和字体产生出了不同种类。这种情况却在秦朝（公元前 221—207 年）秦始皇治下发生了变化。 秦始皇将七个主要城邦统一成了一个整齐划一的国家，其中汉语书写体系开始朝着一个方向发展。这个书写体系对于中国人民和文化的统一有着巨大的重要性。即使在今天，无论中国人住在哪里、说着何种方言，都还能以书写的方式进行交流。 书面汉语，也已成为中国连接现在与过去的重要方式。现代中国人可以读懂古代中国人写的经典作品。对汉语书写体系的高度推崇，可以从汉字作为一种艺术形式的发展中看到；这被称作中国书法艺术，而它已经成为中国文化的一个重要组成部分。 今天，汉语书写体系依然是中国文化的重要组成部分。随着中国在全球事务中扮演的角色变得更为重要，越来越多的国际学生开始透过这种神奇的语言欣赏中国文化和历史。"
    }
  ],
